Description: OpenBSD's net80211 and crypto find PIE's headers, not xnu's
 kext.mk puts the kernel's headers before a kext's own include paths. xnu
 has headers with the names of OpenBSD's sys/mbuf.h, net/if.h, crypto/aes.h
 and others, with other contents. Each include of such a name is quoted, so
 it finds PIE80211Family's compat headers or OpenBSD's crypto headers
 first. Includes of names xnu does not have stay as they are.
Author: The Blueberry Pie OS Authors
Forwarded: not-needed
Last-Update: 2026-11-19

